# MMIO chain census, 2026-09-21 -- taken BEFORE any pass exists, so it
# cannot be tuned to what a pass happens to find (consumer spec 6.1).
#
# instrument: tools/ghidra/MmioChains.java (private tree), Ghidra 12.1.2
#   PUBLIC, snap revision 47 -- the same pin as every oracle run in this arc.
#   It decompiles each function containing a mapping call and walks the
#   high-level P-code varnode graph FORWARD from the call's output.
#
# CORRECTED before banking: the first version reported any load or store
#   the returned pointer REACHED, which conflates the pointer used as an
#   ADDRESS (the device is touched) with the pointer used as a VALUE (it
#   is filed into memory).  On i8042prt the single chain ends at
#   `mov %rcx,0xd0(%rax,%rbx,8)`, where the pointer is the VALUE -- and the
#   first run reported that as an access, which would have been a
#   fabricated claim that a device was touched.  The two are now separate
#   verdicts, MMIOACCESS and MMIOPARKED, and the corrected run is below.
#
# population: the 8 HP drivers.  Denominator printed per driver.

